│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the regime-shift issue directly by making the model rely more on        │
│                          │ short-horizon, normalized, regime-invariant signals and by simplifying XGBoost so it      │
│                          │ prefers robust patterns over regime-specific memorization.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Reduce tree depth and add regularization to prevent overfitting to the training regime. │
│                          │ - Use shorter feature horizons (5-20 bars) and rolling z-scores so the same price/volume  │
│                          │ move is interpreted relative to recent local context.                                     │
│                          │ - Add trend-of-regime features such as changes in volatility and efficiency, which should │
│                          │ generalize better across the test→val shift.                                              │
│                          │ - Add one multiplicative interaction between short momentum and volatility regime, as     │
│                          │ suggested, but in a normalized form.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The feature count stays comfortably below 80, and all features use only past data.        │
