│ patch_description        │ This edit addresses the core problem: val_slope collapse from 0.074→0.006.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Changes:                                                                                  │
│                          │ 1. Reduce primary lookback windows from 60→20 bars (faster decay, better cross-regime     │
│                          │ generalization)                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Add z-score normalized features within rolling windows (makes features                 │
│                          │ regime-invariant)                                                                         │
│                          │ 3. Add volatility trend features (vol_trend_ratio, vol_accel) to detect regime shifts     │
│                          │ 4. Add adaptive momentum scaled by volatility regime                                      │
│                          │ 5. Increase model expressivity: reduce reg_alpha/lambda, increase max_depth from 5→6,     │
│                          │ reduce min_child_weight 1→0.5                                                             │
│                          │ 6. Reduce n_estimators slightly (400→300) to avoid overfitting while increasing depth     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The z-score normalization is crucial: instead of using raw returns, we use (ret -         │
│                          │ rolling_mean) / rolling_std within a window. This makes the feature invariant to the      │
│                          │ absolute volatility level, only capturing deviations from recent behavior.                │
