│ patch_name               │ regime_invariant_short_windows                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the core failure mode: slope collapse on the validation regime. It      │
│                          │ removes several long-horizon, regime-specific features and replaces them with             │
│                          │ shorter-window, rolling z-scored features that are more invariant to volatility regime    │
│                          │ shifts. It also adds rate-of-change regime features and a stronger momentum × volatility  │
│                          │ interaction, which should help the model retain predictive slope in the most recent       │
│                          │ period without inflating feature count.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On the model side, I reduce depth and increase child-weight / regularization slightly     │
│                          │ while using more estimators with a lower learning rate. This typically improves           │
│                          │ out-of-sample stability for XGBoost on noisy crypto perp data and discourages the model   │
│                          │ from memorizing regime-specific splits. The target is to increase val slope and           │
│                          │ prediction dispersion while keeping DA near or above the current floor.                   │
