│ patch_name               │ robust_regime_normalization                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ To solve the val_slope collapse, I am implementing rolling Z-score normalization for all  │
│                          │ scale-dependent features (returns, volatility, volume, trend strength). This makes        │
│                          │ features regime-invariant, as a 'high' value is relative to the recent window rather than │
│                          │ an absolute level.                                                                        │
│                          │ Additionally, I'm simplifying the XGBoost model by reducing max_depth (5 -> 3) and        │
│                          │ significantly increasing min_child_weight (1 -> 12). This prevents the model from fitting │
│                          │ high-frequency noise in the training set that doesn't persist.                            │
│                          │ I also introduced Kaufman's Efficiency Ratio, which is a robust indicator of market       │
│                          │ character (trending vs. ranging) that generalizes well across regimes.                    │
