                        Patch Metadata - Gen 11/150 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 3/3 - Patch: 1/1                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shorter_lookbacks_zscore_norm_vol_adaptive                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This edit addresses the core regime-shift problem by:                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Reducing lookback windows**: Replace 50/60/200 windows with 10/15/20 equivalents.    │
│                          │ 15-min candles move fast; long windows are stale.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Z-score normalization within rolling windows**: For returns and deviations, compute  │
│                          │ (value - rolling_mean) / rolling_std to make features regime-invariant. A 1% return means │
│                          │ different things in vol=0.5% vs vol=2% regimes.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Volatility-adaptive scaling**: Multiply momentum features by vol_trend (fast/slow    │
│                          │ vol ratio) to capture regime-conditional behavior. In low-vol regimes, momentum is        │
│                          │ weaker; in high-vol, it's stronger.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Remove slow regime features**: Drop 200-bar rolling windows and instead use faster   │
│                          │ 20-bar rolling ranks. This reduces stale information.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 5. **Increase model expressivity**: Reduce min_child_weight from 1 to 0.5, increase       │
│                          │ learning_rate from 0.15 to 0.18, increase n_estimators to 500. This allows trees to pick  │
│                          │ up regime-conditional splits better.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 6. **Simpler SMA cross**: Use SMA-10/20 instead of 10/50 for faster mean reversion        │
│                          │ detection.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The result should be:                                                                     │
│                          │ - Higher val_slope (more of train pattern generalizes)                                    │
│                          │ - Higher pred_std_ratio (model is less conservative)                                      │
│                          │ - Better generalization ratio                                                             │
