│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ short_window_regime_features                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the current collapse toward the mean by making the feature set more     │
│                          │ regime-invariant and more reactive to short-lived market structure changes, while also    │
│                          │ giving XGBoost a bit more capacity to use those signals.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Main ideas:                                                                               │
│                          │ - Replace the current longer-horizon volatility regime logic with shorter rolling         │
│                          │ comparisons and rolling z-scores.                                                         │
│                          │ - Add autocorrelation and efficiency-trend features, which capture whether the market is  │
│                          │ becoming more or less trend-like.                                                         │
│                          │ - Keep feature count comfortably below 80.                                                │
│                          │ - Increase model capacity modestly with more trees and slightly less restrictive          │
│                          │ splitting so the model can express a stronger slope on validation without exploding       │
│                          │ overfit.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should help:                                                                     │
│                          │ - The validation regime appears to differ from train/test, so shorter lookbacks and       │
│                          │ normalized signals should survive regime change better.                                   │
│                          │ - The model is currently too flat on validation (`pred_std_ratio` is very low), so a      │
│                          │ little more tree capacity and weaker child-weight constraint should help restore          │
│                          │ prediction dispersion.                                                                    │
│                          │ - The added trend-of-market-character features are designed to capture second-order       │
│                          │ regime shifts rather than just absolute levels.                                           │
