│ patch_description        │ The current model is severely underpredicting variation on the held-out periods, which is │
│                          │ consistent with overly strong regularization and features that are still too tied to a    │
│                          │ single regime. This edit makes two coordinated changes:                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Loosens XGBoost regularization slightly** so the model can express more signal and   │
│                          │ avoid collapsing toward the mean:                                                         │
│                          │    - lower `min_child_weight`                                                             │
│                          │    - lower `reg_alpha` / `reg_lambda`                                                     │
│                          │    - modestly increase depth                                                              │
│                          │    - slightly increase tree count while keeping learning rate moderate                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Rebuilds features around short, rolling, regime-normalized signals**:                │
│                          │    - add short-horizon returns and z-scored returns                                       │
│                          │    - add short volatility levels and volatility trends                                    │
│                          │    - add rolling efficiency/AC-style trend proxies                                        │
│                          │    - add momentum × volatility-regime interaction                                         │
│                          │    - add rolling volume and price-position normalization                                  │
│                          │    - keep the feature count comfortably below 80                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should help the model recover slope on validation by emphasizing faster-decaying     │
│                          │ patterns and regime-relative structure rather than absolute levels.                       │
