│ patch_description        │ The model is currently suffering from severe prediction collapse (val_slope=0.0006,       │
│                          │ pred_std_ratio=0.0146), indicating it is over-regularized and under-expressive.           │
│                          │ 1. Reduced `min_child_weight` (20 -> 5) and `reg_lambda` (10.0 -> 1.0) to allow the model │
│                          │ to make bolder predictions and increase the predictive slope.                             │
│                          │ 2. Increased `max_depth` (4 -> 5) and `learning_rate` (0.05 -> 0.07) to increase model    │
│                          │ expressivity and capture more complex patterns.                                           │
│                          │ 3. Shortened the Z-score normalization window (100 -> 60) to make features more adaptive  │
│                          │ to recent market regimes, which is critical for generalizing across the regime shifts     │
│                          │ observed in the val period.                                                               │
│                          │ 4. Added more return lags [2, 8] and a `vol_trend` feature to capture the rate of change  │
│                          │ in market character.                                                                      │
│                          │ 5. Modified the momentum-volatility interaction to be multiplicative with the volatility  │
│                          │ regime, which often generalizes better than simple division.                              │
